<section class="pub-simple-head"><span class="pub-eyebrow"> StockChief</span><h1><%= heading %></h1><p>Effective <%= kind==='privacy'?'November 23, 2026':'November 18, 2026' %>. StockChief is operated by Keeper Inventory LLC, 13 Austra Pkwy, Monroe, NY 10950, United States.</p></section>
<section class="pub-legal"><% if(kind==='privacy'){ %>
  <h2>1. Scope</h2><p>This notice describes how StockChief handles information when a business evaluates, buys or uses the service. The customer controls the business records and connected accounts placed in its workspace; StockChief processes that data to provide the service.</p>
  <h2>2. Information we process</h2><p>We process account and workspace details, authentication and security events, inventory and operational records, files a user submits, and data received from provider accounts the customer chooses to connect. Connected data may include business email, commerce orders, shipping events, payment status and accounting records.</p>
  <h2>3. How information is used</h2><p>Information is used to authenticate users, operate and secure the service, import business records and keep them in sync, prepare or execute authorized workflows, provide support, process StockChief subscription billing and improve reliability. Privacy-conscious funnel events may measure steps such as demo, pricing, signup, activation and upgrade; the operator can disable that analytics collection.</p>
  <h2>4. AI-assisted processing</h2><p>When an enabled workflow requires language or document interpretation, relevant business content may be sent to the configured AI provider. Deterministic business engines remain responsible for inventory, accounting and action execution. Instructions inside an email or document do not grant authority.</p>
  <p id="google-workspace-limited-use"><strong>Google Workspace Limited Use.</strong> StockChief's use and transfer of raw or derived information received from Google Workspace APIs, including Gmail, will adhere to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a> and the <a href="https://developers.google.com/workspace/workspace-api-user-data-developer-policy">Google Workspace API User Data and Developer Policy</a>, including their Limited Use requirements. Google user data is used only to provide merchant-authorized, user-facing StockChief features. We do not sell this data, use it for advertising, or use or transfer it to create, train or improve foundational or generalized AI/ML models. Relevant business content may be processed by commercial AI API providers solely to deliver the requested feature; provider training and data-sharing programs must not receive Google user data. Customers can disconnect Gmail and request deletion through support.</p>
  <h2>5. Providers and credentials</h2><p>Customers connect their own third-party accounts and can revoke them. OAuth tokens and API credentials are encrypted before storage and are not rendered back into the product. StockChief may use infrastructure, email-delivery, billing and AI providers as service processors; each receives only the data needed for its function.</p>
  <h2>6. Isolation, security and retention</h2><p>Operational records are scoped to a workspace and membership is checked on requests. We use access controls, encrypted transport, protected credential storage and audit records appropriate to the service. Our <a href="/security/data-protection#retention">retention schedule</a> specifies periods, disposal, review of legal holds and recovery copies. Read our <a href="/security/data-protection#prevention">data loss prevention strategy</a> and <a href="/security/data-protection#response">incident response policy</a> for responsibilities and procedures.</p>
  <h2>7. Choices and requests</h2><p>Workspace owners control members, connections and automation authority. They may export business records, disconnect providers and request access, correction or deletion through StockChief support. We use Shopify customer data only for the requested service; we do not sell it or share it for advertising. Shopify order processing uses necessary customer names, email and delivery addresses; customer phone numbers and billing addresses are not imported. Customers may request a person’s review, explain their position and contest a credit hold through the merchant or support. Owners can record manual credit decisions on the customer page on every plan. See <a href="/security/data-protection#purpose">manual processing choices</a>. Provider-side records remain subject to that provider's policies.</p>
  <h2>8. Changes and contact</h2><p>Material changes will be posted here with a new effective date. <% if(supportEmail){ %>Questions or privacy requests may be sent to <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>.<% } else { %>Questions or privacy requests may be submitted through the StockChief support channel available inside the product.<% } %></p>
<% } else { %>
  <h2>1. The service</h2><p>StockChief is business operations software for inventory, purchasing, customer orders, communication, shipping, payments and accounting workflows. Some functions prepare work for approval; functions explicitly authorized by a workspace owner may execute within configured limits.</p>
  <h2>2. Accounts and customer responsibility</h2><p>Customers must provide accurate account information, protect credentials, assign appropriate user roles and maintain lawful authority over all data and provider accounts they connect. The customer remains responsible for reviewing its automation limits, exceptions, tax treatment, accounting policy and legally consequential business decisions.</p>
  <h2>3. Authority and third-party services</h2><p>StockChief does not gain purchasing, communication, payment or shipping authority merely because a provider is connected. Authority is configured separately. Stripe, carriers, email providers, commerce systems and accounting platforms operate under their own terms and may change, delay or reject requests.</p>
  <h2>4. Subscription fees</h2><p>Paid subscriptions renew at the price and billing interval shown before approval, plus applicable taxes and explicitly approved charges. Direct StockChief subscriptions are billed through Stripe. Subscriptions selected through Shopify App Pricing are billed and managed by Shopify, on its displayed billing cycle. StockChief does not receive raw card numbers. Plan &amp; billing identifies your subscription provider and opens that provider’s management page. An existing Stripe subscription is not automatically replaced or charged again through Shopify.</p>
  <h2>5. Money-back guarantee, promotions and plan changes</h2><p>There is no public free trial. Paid access starts after the billing provider confirms the subscription. Shopify development-store test subscriptions may be free; cancelling one returns no money because no payment was taken. You may request a refund within 14 days of your first subscription payment. StockChief records a timely request before contacting the provider. Stripe refunds are submitted through Stripe; eligible Shopify refunds are handled through Shopify’s Partner Dashboard and remain pending until provider evidence confirms the refund. Cancelling renewal alone does not confirm that money was returned. A confirmed subscription refund cancels the subscription and ends operational access. For direct Stripe subscriptions, inventories remain read-only for 30 days before permanent deletion is scheduled. For Shopify subscriptions, export your saved records and contact support to arrange deletion. Export your data before its scheduled deletion date. Account payment receipts and records required for financial or legal obligations are retained. A deletion interrupted by unresolved external work is held until that work is resolved. Promotions may have plan, time, volume or redemption limits. Plan changes use the charges and timing displayed by the subscription provider. A downgrade never silently deletes business history; limits may require the owner to choose which connections or resources remain active.</p>
  <h2>6. Failed payments and cancellation</h2><p>A failed subscription payment enters the configured grace process. After grace, costly or autonomous functions may be suspended while records remain available. Cancellation normally takes effect at the end of the paid term unless checkout or the billing portal says otherwise. Reactivation is subject to successful payment and current plan availability.</p>
  <h2>7. Customer data</h2><p>The customer retains its rights in business data and grants StockChief permission to process it only to provide, secure and support the service. The customer must not submit data it lacks authority to use. Aggregated operational metrics must not identify a customer or disclose its business records.</p>
  <h2>8. Acceptable use</h2><p>Customers may not misuse the service, bypass limits, probe another workspace, upload malicious content, interfere with providers, send unlawful communication or use StockChief to violate law or third-party rights.</p>
  <h2>9. Availability and risk</h2><p>StockChief is designed to preserve evidence and ask rather than guess, but no software eliminates operational risk. Customers should maintain appropriate review, backups, provider access and business continuity procedures. Enterprise service levels apply only when stated in a signed agreement.</p>
  <h2>10. Changes and contact</h2><p>Material changes will be posted with a new effective date. Continued use after the effective date constitutes acceptance where permitted by law. <% if(supportEmail){ %>Questions may be sent to <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>.<% } else { %>Questions may be submitted through the StockChief support channel available inside the product.<% } %></p>
<% } %></section>
